--TEST--
An `array<U>` conversion target whose `U` no runtime tag decides is refused where it is written, because the element walk compares tags and nothing wider, and an enum's help names the per-element `as` on either backing — `rule:types/conversion`, with `rule:enums/representation` and `rule:types/single-value-types` naming two of the types it cannot check
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Cell {
    public function constructor(public string $name) {}
}

enum Rank: int {
    Low = 1,
    High = 2,
}

enum Size: uint {
    Small = 0,
    Large = 40,
}

mixed $m = ["a"];
// A class label is what four bits have no room for, and what a named-class
// binding then reads at a fixed offset — the same type confusion `$foo as Bar`
// is refused for, one container in.
array<Cell> $cells = $m as array<Cell>;
// An enum case's tag names its backing and no enum, so a tag would admit a
// case of every enum with that backing. `as Rank` on one element checks the
// value against the cases of `Rank`, and the help says so.
array<Rank> $ranks = $m as array<Rank>;
array<Size> $sizes = $m as array<Size>;
// A union admits some values of its representation and not others, which is
// again more than a tag says. `mixed` is the one that is accepted, because it
// admits all of them.
array<?string> $maybes = $m as array<?string>;
// The refusal reads through every level, and names the level that failed.
array<array<Cell>> $nested = $m as array<array<Cell>>;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0711]: `array<Cell>` cannot be an `as` target
%A
error[E0711]: `array<Rank>` cannot be an `as` target
%A
   = help: `as` checks each element at run time, and that check only sees what kind of value the element is. The cases of every enum backed by `int` are the same kind of value, so the check cannot tell `Rank` from another enum. Convert to `array<mixed>`, then use `as Rank` on each element you read. That checks the element against the cases of `Rank`.

error[E0711]: `array<Size>` cannot be an `as` target
%A
   = help: `as` checks each element at run time, and that check only sees what kind of value the element is. The cases of every enum backed by `uint` are the same kind of value, so the check cannot tell `Size` from another enum. Convert to `array<mixed>`, then use `as Size` on each element you read. That checks the element against the cases of `Size`.

error[E0711]: `array<string|null>` cannot be an `as` target
%A
error[E0711]: `array<array<Cell>>` cannot be an `as` target
%A
error: aborting due to 5 errors
